<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Leave</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>leave</a>
<a cmd='#'>exit</a>
</pre>
<p>To move around in the world you just type the direction. But when you are
inside something, like a boat, a cart or a barrel you climbed into (see
<a cmd='#'>Help Enter</a>), leave or exit gets you out of it again, into the place around
it.
</p><p>The two differ when your boat or cart, or the steed you ride, is itself
inside something (you can take them along when you enter some places):
leave takes you out together with it, while exit gets you out of the boat
or cart and leaves it behind.
</p><p>You must be standing, not fighting, and the thing must be open. To get off
a steed, dismount (see <a cmd='#'>Help Mount</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Enter</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Exits</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Boats</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Mount</a>
</pre>




</div>